# The ONE lab env file: every key and setting lives here. Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and edit.
# Format: NAME=value, no quotes, no spaces around the equals sign. Values starting with ./ or ../ are
# resolved relative to this file's folder. Never commit `.env`.
# Run any command with these loaded (nothing is printed):
#   pwsh -NoProfile -File .claude/skills/security-git/scripts/run-with-env.ps1 -- <command> <args>
# A line left as `your_key_here` or empty is skipped, so you only fill in what you use.

# --- API keys ---
# Data Commons API key (free: https://apikeys.datacommons.org). Used only by the Data Commons MCP
# server admission review (board task T-0048).
DC_API_KEY=your_key_here

# --- The single source catalog: what each external source permits, and its API settings ---
# The evidence skill, the fetcher and agents all read this one file. Edit it there, nowhere else.
EVIDENCE_CATALOG=../cf-research/sources/catalog.yaml
# Optional contact address added to the evidence tool's user agent (publishers ask for one).
# EVIDENCE_CONTACT=you@example.org

# --- Local model ---
# Your preferred local model (an Ollama model name). If this is unset and no profile is set, there is
# no local worker and ALL work is cloud-only; nothing falls back to a particular model.
# Delete the leading # and use the exact name `ollama list` shows after YOU pull a model. The lab's own choice is
# qwen3.8:27b; the lab's measured profiles also use a local alias (qwen3.8:27b-64k) that `ollama pull` does not give you
# (a person makes it with `ollama create`; recipe in docs/local-models-ollama.md).
# LOCAL_WORKER_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b
# Optional sampling profiles. The fast profile is used for the first attempts of a delegated task, the
# thinking profile for the last one. A profile's model and num_ctx are sent with every request.
# Start a path with ./ so it is resolved relative to this file; without ./ it is relative to the folder
# the command runs in. LOCAL_WORKER_MODEL, if set, replaces the profile's model name (num_ctx still comes
# from the profile), so leave it unset or give it the same name as the profile.
# Portable 32K pair (needs only `ollama pull qwen3.8:27b`):
# LOCAL_WORKER_PROFILE=./.claude/skills/model-qwen3-8-27b/ollama-profile.fast.json
# LOCAL_WORKER_THINKING_PROFILE=./.claude/skills/model-qwen3-8-27b/ollama-profile.json
# The lab machine's 64K pair (chosen by the maintainer 2026-10-10; needs the qwen3.8:27b-64k alias, and the
# maintainer sets these in their own .env, with LOCAL_WORKER_MODEL=qwen3.8:27b-64k or that line left unset):
# LOCAL_WORKER_PROFILE=./.claude/skills/model-qwen3-8-27b/ollama-profile.64k.fast.json
# LOCAL_WORKER_THINKING_PROFILE=./.claude/skills/model-qwen3-8-27b/ollama-profile.64k.json

# --- Cloud delegation (off unless true; see AGENTS.md) ---
# COUNCIL_CROSS_PROVIDER_DELEGATION=false

# --- Local files (optional) ---
# The untracked cf-lab-files folder next to this repo, made by setup.cmd or setup.sh.
# Scripts that need it read this; agents find it through AGENTS.md. Never put keys or patient data in it.
# LAB_FILES=../cf-lab-files
